# fieldtrip-mex-excludes
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared rsync exclusion rules for legacy and unsupported MEX platform
# extensions. Referenced by both the main FieldTrip sync (.github/fieldtrip-
# sync-filters) and the per-package external syncs in the workflow.
#
# Synced:   mexa64     Linux 64-bit
#           mexmaca64  macOS Apple Silicon (arm64)
#           mexmaci64  macOS Intel 64-bit
#           mexw64     Windows 64-bit
#
# Protected: bem_*.mexmaca64, SPM's own Apple Silicon build of external/bemcp,
#           which FieldTrip does not ship, survives --delete. Upstream copies
#           would still update it. Other mexmaca64 files follow upstream,
#           deletions included. Remove once FieldTrip ships bem_*.mexmaca64
#           (fieldtrip/fieldtrip#2496).
#
# Excluded: mexw32     Windows 32-bit (end-of-life)
#           mexglx     Linux 32-bit (end-of-life)
#           mexlx      Linux legacy (end-of-life)
#           mexsol     Solaris (end-of-life)
#           mexmac     macOS pre-Intel (end-of-life)
#           mexmaci    macOS Intel 32-bit (end-of-life; mexmaci64 is kept)
#           *.mex      bare suffix — local build artifact with no platform tag
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
P bem_*.mexmaca64
- *.mexw32
- *.mexglx
- *.mexlx
- *.mexsol
- *.mexmac
- *.mexmaci
- *.mex
